{
  "scope": "ClientboundLevelChunkPacketData and nested BlockEntityInfo wire readers and writers, all 14 release families",
  "findings": [
    "Heightmap NBT (763\u2013769) uses the nullable compound reader followed by an explicit null rejection. The old Rust codec rejected null correctly but incorrectly accepted non-compound roots.",
    "Embedded block-entity NBT uses the nullable compound reader in all 14 release families, including 766\u2013776. The old Rust codec incorrectly accepted non-compound roots.",
    "The new checks reject non-compound roots before parsing their payloads and reject non-compound values on encode. TAG_End remains supported for embedded block entities, without importing the stricter standalone tile_entity_data 766 boundary."
